3. What is ported into this module
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Nothing is a verbatim Swift copy. The Swift tree is not vendored. Behaviour,
wire formats, byte tables and the bundled certificate are ported into original
Kotlin. Fill this list as each lot lands:

  Lot A4 (NFC ISO 15693)      <- LibreCRKit NFCActivationCommand.swift,
                                 NFCActivationModels.swift, Libre3ReceiverID.swift
                                 (planned, not written yet)
  Lot A5 (crypto)             <- LibreCRKit LibAES.swift, AESCCM.swift,
                                 SessionKey.swift, ChallengeMessage.swift,
                                 Phase5KeySchedule.swift, PhoneCert.swift,
                                 DataPlaneCrypto.swift, Resources/RuntimeTables
                                 (planned, not written yet)
  Lot A6 (BLE session)        <- LibreCRKit LibreSensorGATT.swift,
                                 PairingFlow.swift; LibreLoop
                                 LibreLoopPairingService.swift,
                                 LibreLoopSensorMonitor.swift,
                                 LibreLoopKeychain.swift
                                 (planned, not written yet)
  Lot A7 (parse / ingest)     <- LibreCRKit RealtimeGlucoseReading.swift,
                                 PatchStatus.swift, DataPlaneDecoder.swift,
                                 SensorLifecycle.swift
                                 (planned, not written yet)

Binary artifacts that will be embedded (all from the MIT LibreCRKit tree,
Sources/LibreCRKit/Resources/RuntimeTables):

  phone_cert_162b.bin (162 bytes, family prefix 03 03) — the phone certificate
  sent during first pairing. The sibling phone_cert_firstpair.bin (prefix 03 00)
  is rejected by live sensors and must not be used.
  libaes_*.bin — the table banks for the Phase 5 wire block primitive.

Upstream states that these tables were produced by clean-room research on
Abbott's own library and that they are fixed across users and installs. See
section 5 for the honest risk note.


-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
4. What is NOT in this module
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  * No Abbott shared object (.so), no Abbott APK content, no Abbott binary of
    any kind is shipped or loaded.
  * No Juggluco source (Java, C++, tables, cert loaders). Juggluco is named in
    user-facing text only as an app to close before connecting; that is not code
    derivation.
  * No Libre 2 / Libre 2 Plus protocol code, and no Libre 2 UUIDs.
  * No Dexcom, Eversense or xDrip code. The Dexcom ONE+ module was used as a
    module shape template (Gradle, plugin shell, activity shape) only; that code
    is this fork's own work and stays under AGPL-3.


